{"id":"87daa22c-72da-41c2-80fd-a055f74a7381","object":"chat.completion","created":1785001417,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate structure\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('case must be a dict')\\n    tokens = case.get('tokens')\\n    calls = case.get('calls')\\n    if not isinstance(tokens, list) or not all(isinstance(t, str) for t in tokens):\\n        raise ValueError('tokens must be a list of strings')\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError('calls must be a list')\\n    for c in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(c, dict):\\n            raise ValueError('each call must be a dict')\\n        for key in ('call_id', 'start', 'end', 'score', 'replacement_tokens'):\\n            if key not in c:\\n                raise ValueError(f'missing key {key} in call')\\n        if not isinstance(c['call_id'], str):\\n            raise ValueError('call_id must be string')\\n        if not isinstance(c['start'], int) or not isinstance(c['end'], int):\\n            raise ValueError('start and end must be int')\\n        if not isinstance(c['score'], (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError('score must be numeric')\\n        if not isinstance(c['replacement_tokens'], list) or not all(isinstance(rt, str) for rt in c['replacement_tokens']):\\n            raise ValueError('replacement_tokens must be list of strings')\\n        if not (0 <= c['start'] < c['end'] <= len(tokens)):\\n            raise ValueError('invalid interval')\\n\\n    # Sort by descending score, then ascending start, then ascending call_id (lexicographic)\\n    sorted_calls = sorted(calls, key=lambda c: (-c['score'], c['start'], c['call_id']))\\n\\n    selected = []  # list of (start, end, call_id)\\n    for c in sorted_calls:\\n        overlap = False\\n        for s, e, _ in selected:\\n            if not (c['end'] <= s or c['start'] >= e):\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            selected.append((c['start'], c['end'], c['call_id']))\\n\\n    # Sort selected by start for reporting order\\n    selected.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\\n    selected_call_ids = [call_id for _, _, call_id in selected]\\n\\n    # Apply replacements right to left\\n    final_tokens = tokens[:]\\n    for start, end, call_id in sorted(selected, key=lambda x: -x[0]):\\n        # Find the call dict to get replacement_tokens\\n        # Since we have unique call_id, we can map\\n        # But easier: rebuild mapping from calls\\n        # Actually we need to get replacement_tokens for this call\\n        # Better to store more info in selected\\n        pass\\n\\n    # Re-design: keep call dict in selected\\n    selected_calls = []\\n    for c in sorted_calls:\\n        overlap = False\\n        for sc in selected_calls:\\n            if not (c['end'] <= sc['start'] or c['start'] >= sc['end']):\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            selected_calls.append(c)\\n\\n    # Sort by start for output\\n    selected_calls.sort(key=lambda c: c['start'])\\n    selected_call_ids = [c['call_id'] for c in selected_calls]\\n\\n    # Apply replacements right to left by start descending\\n    final_tokens = tokens[:]\\n    for c in sorted(selected_calls, key=lambda c: -c['start']):\\n        final_tokens[c['start']:c['end']] = c['replacement_tokens']\\n\\n    return {\\n        'selected_call_ids': selected_call_ids,\\n        'tokens': final_tokens\\n    }\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to write solve(case) that processes a case payload with tokens and calls. The objective: interleave tokens with replacement tokens from accepted calls, selecting calls greedily by descending score, then start, then call_id. Overlap rejection: if a call overlaps any already selected call, reject it. Then apply replacements from right to left to avoid offset shifts. Return selected_call_ids (list of call_ids in order of their start positions) and tokens (the final interleaved list).\n\nInput case is a dict with \"tokens\" (list of strings) and \"calls\" (list of dicts with call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens). The start and end are indices? In fixture, start and end are integers presumably referring to token indices. end is exclusive? In example: start=1, end=3 for call a (tokens indices 1,2). That's typical. So we need to handle that.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: tokens must be list, calls list of dict with required keys.\n2. Sort calls by priority: descending score, then ascending start, then ascending call_id (string comparison? call_id is string, should compare lexicographically? In specification: \"call ID\" likely string compare. Use standard lexicographic order for tie-breaker.\n3. Greedy selection: iterate sorted calls, check if selected set has any overlapping with current (overlap defined as intervals [start, end) that intersect). Use simple condition: if call.end <= selected.start or call.start >= selected.end for all selected? Actually better to track intervals and check if new interval overlaps any existing. Since we process sorted by priority, we can keep list of selected intervals. For each call, check if its start < selected_end and its end > selected_start for any selected. If no overlap, add to selected list.\n4. After selection, sort selected calls by start (ascending). That gives selected_call_ids in order of start.\n5. Apply replacements from right to left on tokens: for each selected call in reverse order of start (descending), replace tokens[start:end] with replacement_tokens. Since we go right to left, offsets of earlier calls are unaffected.\n6. Return dict with selected_call_ids and tokens (the final list).\n\nEdge cases: replacement_tokens could be empty list? Probably not but handle. Overlap check: use [start, end) intervals. Ensure end > start.\n\nReturn only the two keys as per schema. No additional.\n\nNow write Python function.\n\nCheck fixture: tokens list length 10, calls with start/end within [0,10). Also there is \"_case_nonce\" not used.\n\nImplement solve(case) accordingly.\n\nWrite code with proper validation: raise ValueError if missing keys or invalid types.\n\nReturn dict.\n\nNow produce JSON output with key \"implementation\" and the source code as string.\n\nMake sure to escape properly."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1654,"completion_tokens":1496,"total_tokens":3150,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":601},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":118},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}